{
  "name": "send_mail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Transform the following news items into an HTML newsletter ready to be sent by email.\n\nPRIORITY PERSONALIZATION INSTRUCTION:\nYou MUST adapt your writing style, adjust the choice of topics, or apply the specific instructions requested by the user below. If this variable contains text, follow it; otherwise, ignore this line:\n{{ $('Get Users Infos').item.json.Personalized_prompt }}\n\nTITLES:\n{{ $json.concatenated_title }}\n\nLINKS:\n{{ $json.concatenated_link }}\n\nCONTENTS:\n{{ $json.concatenated_content }}\n\nInstructions:\n\n-Generate a complete newsletter in HTML email format.\n-The result must be beautiful, responsive, and readable on mobile.\n-You must include the unsubscribe link at the bottom of the email.\n-The link text must be: Unsubscribe from the newsletter.\n-Return only the final HTML.",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "=You are an expert professional newsletter writer and HTML email integrator.\n\nYour mission is to transform raw news items into a complete, clear, modern HTML newsletter that is ready to be sent by email.\n\nYou must produce only valid HTML.\nDo not produce Markdown.\nDo not produce a code block.\nDo not provide any explanation before or after the HTML.\n\nObjective:\nCreate a professional newsletter, responsive and readable on both desktop and mobile, with a clean, modern, and pleasant design.\n\nWriting rules:\n\n-Summarize the articles accurately, without inventing information.\n-Keep a serious, professional, dynamic, and pleasant tone.\n-Use short and clear sentences.\n-Avoid large blocks of text.\n-Each news item must include a link to its source.\n-If a source or content is insufficient, remain cautious in the wording.\n-Include minimum 5 articles in the newsletter.\n\nHTML email rules:\n\n-Generate a complete email-compatible HTML structure.\n-Mainly use HTML tables for layout.\n-Use inline CSS.\n-Maximum container width: 640px.\n-Light general background.\n-White central container with rounded corners.\n-Clean design with a professional blue as the main color.\n-Visible buttons for source links.\n-No JavaScript.\n-No Markdown.\n-No fake links.\n-No text outside the HTML.\n\nMandatory structure:\n\n1. Header:\n\n   -Name: Persona\n   -Subtitle: Your personalized news letter\n\n2. Main title:\n\n   -Catchy and professional\n   -Maximum 10 words\n\n3. Introduction:\n\n   -2 to 3 lines maximum\n   -Presents the overall context of the news\n\n4. “Key takeaways” section:\n\n   -Maximum 3 key points\n   -Short and readable format\n\n5. News items:\n   For each news item, create an HTML card containing:\n\n   -A short title\n   -A 3 to 4 sentence summary\n   -A “Read the source” button with the corresponding source link\n\n6. GDPR footer:\n\n   -Indicate that the user receives this newsletter because they subscribed to Persona.\n   -Add a clear unsubscribe link.\n   -Unsubscribe link: `<a href=\"{{ \"http://localhost:5678/webhook/unsubscribe?email=\" + encodeURIComponent($('Loop Over Items').item.json.email) }}\">Unsubscribe from the newsletter</a>`\n\nFinal constraints:\n\n-The final output must be directly usable in the HTML field of an n8n Email node.\n-Never display raw variables.\n-Never invent a source.\n-Never generate Markdown."
        }
      },
